# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added when the repo was first put under version control (port work).
#
# Rule of thumb: track the SOURCES and the RECOMPILER INPUTS (the .json tables
# that decide what gets translated and how it is bound). Everything else below
# is build output, third-party tooling, a debug artifact, or copyrighted game
# content that must not live in version control.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- third-party tooling (large, re-downloadable) --------------------------
# vendor/* rather than vendor/, because git cannot re-include anything under a
# directory it has already excluded -- and vendor/lua/ has to be tracked. It is
# not tooling: it is a build dependency the executable links, so a clone that
# did not have it would not compile. Same reasoning as fmidi-master/ and
# discord-rpc-master/, which are tracked for the same reason.
vendor/*
!vendor/lua/
!vendor/dr_mp3.h
tools/dolphin/
tools/our_build/
_rgh_stale/
*.zip

# --- copyrighted game content ----------------------------------------------
# The DOL, the RSO/ELF dumps and the extracted assets are retail game data.
# They are inputs supplied locally, they never change, and committing them
# would make this repo undistributable. Keep a separate backup of these.
Assets/
# splash/ is deliberately NOT under Assets/: everything under Assets/ is game
# data, and an exception carved out of that rule is how game data gets committed
# by accident. The splash artwork is ours and IS tracked, at splash/.
# Extracted FROM Assets/ by tools/extract_brfna.py, so it is retail game data
# wearing a .h extension. CMake regenerates it when missing.
src/robox_font_a8.h
src/robox_font_metrics.h
# Same problem, different tool. wii_font_* came out of a dumped game texture
# (tools/extract_font.py reads tex_0068_va90f28240_256x256_fmt14.png) and
# wii_death_wav.h is a ripped system sound -- 1.2 MB of retail data between
# them, wearing .h extensions exactly like the two above.
#
# These were committed once and have since been untracked. They are still in
# the history, so rewriting it is the only way to remove them completely.
src/wii_font_rgba.h
src/wii_font_metrics.h
src/wii_death_wav.h

# Mod data, all of it derived or third-party:
#   robox.dls  built from Assets/music/robox.wt + robox.pcm by sdk/robox_dls.c
#              on first run, so it never needs to be committed
#   mario.chr  SMB1 character data
#   wavs/      user music packs, whatever they happen to contain
# The .cfg defaults ARE ours and stay tracked -- see the negations.
#
# mods/lua/ is the exception: those are OUR example mods and the documentation
# for the scripting API is written against them, so they ship. What a mod
# writes at runtime does not -- .cache/ is the merged script/game.lua the guest
# bridge generates, and the .cfg files are whatever a player has toggled.
mods/*
!mods/mods.cfg
!mods/wav_music.cfg
!mods/lua/
mods/lua/**/.cache/
mods/lua/*.cfg
mods/lua/**/config.cfg

# Baked by tools/bin2c.py at configure time from sources that ARE committed
# (Setup/*.rbxs, mods/*.cfg, splash/*). Just hex derived from them.
src/generated_setup/

